        // set wagers[player] = msg.value, but the intended rule here is to ensure consistency between the
        // recorded wager and the actual sent amount. The reference C always preserves this equality for any input
        // where wager() succeeded; the mutant changes admissible successes (allowing different msg.value to pass)
        // which leads to behavior differences across inputs. We observe that equality via the public hasPlayerWagered +
        // direct call to the mapping via currentBetLimit and hasPlayerWagered isn't enough, but wagers is private.
        // However, we can read whether player has wagered and the contract exposes wagers only via hasPlayerWagered.
        // To check the actual stored amount we rely on the fact that winnersPot() == address(c).balance / 2 and
